Subject: [PATCH 03/16] Add Request via Seerr fallback stream + retry-on-401
 auto re-auth

- addon.js: fallback stream serves a static placeholder video via /request
  instead of externalUrl (always opens outside app) or a blocking
  poll/redirect design (both proven broken by real player HTTP timeout
  and redirect-count limits - see DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md section 13)
- server.js: /request submits to Seerr then immediately responds with
  assets/requested-placeholder.mp4 (generated via ffmpeg). No polling,
  no redirect loop - user manually reopens the title once downloaded.
- seerr.js: Seerr client, IMDb->TMDb resolution via TMDb /find endpoint
- jellyfin.js: retry-on-401 auto re-authentication for all API calls,
  fixing a full-addon regression where a stale Jellyfin session token
  caused every stream request to fail until manually restarted

Known issue (documented, unresolved): the fallback stream displays
correctly in Nuvio but not in Stremio's own client - confirmed not a
server-side or stremio-core issue via source review, likely a
stremio-web UI-layer filter not yet located.
